Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.52,0:00:22.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,本期《造物小百科》……
Dialogue: 1,0:00:21.52,0:00:22.32,Original,,0,0,0,,On how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.24,0:00:26.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,助听器
Dialogue: 1,0:00:26.24,0:00:26.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Hearing aids.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.60,0:00:31.02,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今的助听器已经小巧到可以隐藏起来
Dialogue: 1,0:00:27.60,0:00:31.02,Original,,0,0,0,,The modern device has now become small enough to be discreet
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.02,0:00:34.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,随着科技进步，它们终于迎来了自己的春天
Dialogue: 1,0:00:31.02,0:00:34.48,Original,,0,0,0,,and with technological advances, they have at last come into their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.56,0:00:37.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,三维拼图
Dialogue: 1,0:00:36.56,0:00:37.60,Original,,0,0,0,,3D puzzles.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.32,0:00:41.02,Translation,,0,0,0,,传统消遣进入新维度
Dialogue: 1,0:00:38.32,0:00:41.02,Original,,0,0,0,,A traditional pastime enters a new dimension.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.24,0:00:46.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,多达1500块三维拼片，可上下甚至侧向拼接
Dialogue: 1,0:00:41.24,0:00:46.20,Original,,0,0,0,,With 1500 3D pieces that fit up, down, and even sideways.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.92,0:00:48.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,胶垫
Dialogue: 1,0:00:47.92,0:00:48.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Rubber mats.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.12,0:00:52.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,废旧轮胎堆积如山，一直饱受诟病，这理所当然
Dialogue: 1,0:00:49.12,0:00:52.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Used tire mountains have had a bad press, and rightly so.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.80,0:00:56.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,当然，消除废物的最好办法就是回收利用
Dialogue: 1,0:00:52.80,0:00:56.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Of course, the best way to eradicate waste is to recycle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.60,0:00:58.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有抽水马桶
Dialogue: 1,0:00:57.60,0:00:58.16,Original,,0,0,0,,And toilets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.88,0:01:01.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,250年来，我们一直视它为理所当然
Dialogue: 1,0:00:58.88,0:01:01.68,Original,,0,0,0,,For 250 years, we've taken them for granted,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.08,0:01:03.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,但你还会想用旱厕吗？
Dialogue: 1,0:01:02.08,0:01:03.84,Original,,0,0,0,,but would you still want to use a latrine?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.96,0:01:08.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过首先，尽管它们优点不少
Dialogue: 1,0:01:04.96,0:01:08.08,Original,,0,0,0,,But first, despite their qualities,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.40,0:01:12.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,自问世以来，助听器就一直不受聋人和听障人士待见
Dialogue: 1,0:01:08.40,0:01:12.80,Original,,0,0,0,,they've remained unloved by the deaf and hearing impaired since their invention.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.68,0:01:17.78,Translation,,0,0,0,,但如今的助听器已变得足够小巧可隐蔽佩戴
Dialogue: 1,0:01:13.68,0:01:17.78,Original,,0,0,0,,But the modern hearing aid has now become small enough to be discreet
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.44,0:01:23.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,再加上科技进步，它们终于迎来了自己的春天
Dialogue: 1,0:01:18.44,0:01:23.04,Original,,0,0,0,,and with technological advances. They have at last come into their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.56,0:01:30.38,Translation,,0,0,0,,无论是天生失聪，还是后天听力受损
Dialogue: 1,0:01:26.56,0:01:30.38,Original,,0,0,0,,Whether hearing impaired from birth or through loss later in life
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.38,0:01:34.30,Translation,,0,0,0,,失聪都是沉重打击，需要时间慢慢适应
Dialogue: 1,0:01:30.38,0:01:34.30,Original,,0,0,0,,deafness can be a massive blow, and takes time to adjust to.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.20,0:01:39.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,助听器让成千上万的人能听到或多或少的声响
Dialogue: 1,0:01:35.20,0:01:39.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Hearing aids offer to thousands the ability to hear to some degree or other
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.72,0:01:43.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,但在制作之前，必须先进行听力测试
Dialogue: 1,0:01:39.72,0:01:43.04,Original,,0,0,0,,but before construction begins, a hearing test is needed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.68,0:01:47.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,听力计检测患者的听力，并生成报告
Dialogue: 1,0:01:43.68,0:01:47.20,Original,,0,0,0,,An audiometer tests the patient's hearing, and a report is produced.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.56,0:01:50.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来，为耳道制作印模
Dialogue: 1,0:01:48.56,0:01:50.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Next, a mould of the ear canal is made.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.76,0:01:54.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,注入硅胶液，做出耳道印模
Dialogue: 1,0:01:51.76,0:01:54.56,Original,,0,0,0,,A silicon liquid is administered to create an impression.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.20,0:01:57.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,等它凝固后，小心地取出
Dialogue: 1,0:01:55.20,0:01:57.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Once solidified, it's carefully removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.76,0:02:06.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块凝固的胶块是耳道的完美复制品
Dialogue: 1,0:02:03.76,0:02:06.80,Original,,0,0,0,,This congealed mass, a perfect replica of the canal,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.04,0:02:10.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,再浸入温蜡中，得到阳模
Dialogue: 1,0:02:07.04,0:02:10.08,Original,,0,0,0,,is then soaked in warm wax to obtain a positive imprint.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.80,0:02:22.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后往容器里灌入硅胶
Dialogue: 1,0:02:20.80,0:02:22.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the container is filled with silicon,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.84,0:02:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,它只要10分钟就会凝固
Dialogue: 1,0:02:23.84,0:02:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,which hardens in only 10 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.92,0:02:29.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,取出已凝固的硅胶块
Dialogue: 1,0:02:27.92,0:02:29.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The hardened silicon block is removed,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.00,0:02:34.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,去除多余部分，只保留关键部位
Dialogue: 1,0:02:30.00,0:02:34.40,Original,,0,0,0,,And any excess eradicated, so that only the essential part is retained.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.36,0:02:37.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,印模必须能轻松滑入耳道
Dialogue: 1,0:02:35.36,0:02:37.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The imprint must slip easily into the ear.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.96,0:02:40.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在进入助听器的成型阶段
Dialogue: 1,0:02:38.96,0:02:40.96,Original,,0,0,0,,It's now the moulding stage for the hearing aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.44,0:02:45.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,往模具中注入亚克力，然后放入这台紫外线烘箱
Dialogue: 1,0:02:41.44,0:02:45.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Acrylic is poured into the mould before placing it into this ultraviolet oven.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.08,0:02:49.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台烘箱不发热，却能让亚克力变硬
Dialogue: 1,0:02:46.08,0:02:49.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Without emitting any heat, this oven hardens the acrylic.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.24,0:02:54.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,此时，助听器外壳还没有装入电子元件
Dialogue: 1,0:02:50.24,0:02:54.16,Original,,0,0,0,,At this point, the raw prosthesis is without its electrical components.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.96,0:02:57.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这张图纸详细标出了放大器的电路
Dialogue: 1,0:02:54.96,0:02:57.92,Original,,0,0,0,,This plan details the electric circuit of the amplifier.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.04,0:03:01.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,为音量旋钮钻孔
Dialogue: 1,0:02:59.04,0:03:01.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Holes are pierced for the volume control.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.56,0:03:04.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些元件极为微小
Dialogue: 1,0:03:03.56,0:03:04.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The components are minuscule.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.68,0:03:07.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这就是音量旋钮
Dialogue: 1,0:03:05.68,0:03:07.20,Original,,0,0,0,,This is the volume control.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.08,0:03:12.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,捕捉声音的微型麦克风
Dialogue: 1,0:03:10.08,0:03:12.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The miniature microphone that captures the sounds,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.68,0:03:16.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,以及充当扬声器的受话器
Dialogue: 1,0:03:13.68,0:03:16.08,Original,,0,0,0,,and the earphone which functions as a speaker.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.60,0:03:22.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,这根由7股导线编成的细线
Dialogue: 1,0:03:19.60,0:03:22.96,Original,,0,0,0,,This tiny braided wire of 7 conductors is soldered
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.04,0:03:26.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,用焊锡焊到放大器和外壳其他部件上
Dialogue: 1,0:03:23.04,0:03:26.08,Original,,0,0,0,,to the amplifier and other parts of the prosthesis with pewter.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.60,0:03:33.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,电路板装入硅胶护套中加以保护
Dialogue: 1,0:03:29.60,0:03:33.52,Original,,0,0,0,,The hybrid circuit is inserted into a silicon casing which protects it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.80,0:03:40.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后把导线焊到受话器上
Dialogue: 1,0:03:38.80,0:03:40.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the wires are soldered to the speaker,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.56,0:03:47.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,并检查音量旋钮是否工作正常
Dialogue: 1,0:03:44.56,0:03:47.52,Original,,0,0,0,,and they verify the proper functioning of the volume control.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.80,0:03:51.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,助听器必须非常隐蔽
Dialogue: 1,0:03:48.80,0:03:51.12,Original,,0,0,0,,A hearing aid must be very discreet.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.60,0:03:54.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,因此用金刚石锯片切掉多余部分
Dialogue: 1,0:03:51.60,0:03:54.16,Original,,0,0,0,,That's why they cut the excess with a diamond disc.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.20,0:03:58.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,还用细砂纸打磨掉毛糙处
Dialogue: 1,0:03:55.20,0:03:58.08,Original,,0,0,0,,They also remove any roughness with fine sandpaper.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.96,0:04:02.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里看到的孔是用来给受话器通气的
Dialogue: 1,0:03:58.96,0:04:02.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The holes we see here are used to vent air from the earphone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.80,0:04:05.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,用这根硅胶管制作通气孔
Dialogue: 1,0:04:02.80,0:04:05.12,Original,,0,0,0,,This silicon tube is used to make the vent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.04,0:04:09.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,往管中注入亚克力，形成一条通道
Dialogue: 1,0:04:07.04,0:04:09.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Acrylic is poured into the tube to form a tunnel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.72,0:04:13.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,用紫外线使亚克力硬化
Dialogue: 1,0:04:10.72,0:04:13.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Ultraviolet light is used to harden the acrylic.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.68,0:04:15.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后取出硅胶管
Dialogue: 1,0:04:13.68,0:04:15.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Afterwards, the tube is removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.84,0:04:23.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,这个孔用于固定拉线
Dialogue: 1,0:04:21.84,0:04:23.84,Original,,0,0,0,,This hole is used to position the fastener,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.84,0:04:28.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,这根细线便于把助听器从耳中取出
Dialogue: 1,0:04:23.84,0:04:28.24,Original,,0,0,0,,a small wire which allows for the removal of the hearing aid from the ear.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.84,0:04:35.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后装入电池
Dialogue: 1,0:04:33.84,0:04:35.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the battery is installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.00,0:04:39.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,只剩下少数零件，如麦克风，还未就位
Dialogue: 1,0:04:36.00,0:04:39.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Only a few parts, such as the microphone. remain to be put in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.08,0:04:43.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后所有零件被小心翼翼地装入外壳内部
Dialogue: 1,0:04:40.08,0:04:43.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Then everything is delicately assembled into the interior of the prosthesis.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.88,0:04:51.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后把助听器两半粘合在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:04:48.88,0:04:51.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The 2 parts of the hearing aid are then glued together.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.00,0:04:55.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,再次用紫外线使胶水固化
Dialogue: 1,0:04:52.00,0:04:55.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Again, ultraviolet is used as it hardens the glue.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.20,0:05:05.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,用钻头切掉用于固定外壳零件的定位板
Dialogue: 1,0:05:01.20,0:05:05.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The plate used to position the prosthesis components is cut away with a drill.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.84,0:05:10.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后手工打磨助听器，使其表面光滑、佩戴舒适
Dialogue: 1,0:05:05.84,0:05:10.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the hearing aid is manually polished to make it perfectly smooth and comfortable.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.64,0:05:21.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,助听器外壳制作完成
Dialogue: 1,0:05:19.64,0:05:21.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The prosthesis is now completed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.32,0:05:24.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,还剩一个重要步骤：
Dialogue: 1,0:05:22.32,0:05:24.08,Original,,0,0,0,,There remains one important step:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.72,0:05:27.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,检验它的电声特性
Dialogue: 1,0:05:24.72,0:05:27.28,Original,,0,0,0,,verifying its electroacoustic characteristic.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.00,0:05:30.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,用这台分析仪验证助听器
Dialogue: 1,0:05:28.00,0:05:30.16,Original,,0,0,0,,It's with this analyzer that they validate that the
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.16,0:05:32.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,是否符合最初的验配处方
Dialogue: 1,0:05:30.16,0:05:32.72,Original,,0,0,0,,hearing aid conforms to the original prescription.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.08,0:05:43.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些微型装置是改善听力的关键
Dialogue: 1,0:05:40.08,0:05:43.52,Original,,0,0,0,,These minute devices are key to improving one's sense
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.52,0:05:47.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,数字技术又正好适合这一领域
Dialogue: 1,0:05:43.52,0:05:47.84,Original,,0,0,0,,of hearing, and with digital technology perfectly suited to this field
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.84,0:05:50.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,希望未来能造出更小的助听器
Dialogue: 1,0:05:47.84,0:05:50.96,Original,,0,0,0,,hopefully even smaller units will be created.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.48,0:06:06.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,拼图曾是周日消磨时光的传统活动
Dialogue: 1,0:06:02.48,0:06:06.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Jigsaw puzzles used to be a Sunday activity to wile away the long hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.60,0:06:09.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过，请把那个印象忘掉
Dialogue: 1,0:06:07.60,0:06:09.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Well, put that image out of your mind,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.72,0:06:13.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,因为如今的精密拼图可以有
Dialogue: 1,0:06:10.72,0:06:13.12,Original,,0,0,0,,because today's sophisticated puzzles can have
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.36,0:06:21.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,1500块三维拼片，可上下甚至侧向拼接
Dialogue: 1,0:06:13.36,0:06:21.04,Original,,0,0,0,,1500 3D pieces that fit up, down, and even sideways.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.28,0:06:25.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,平面拼图人人皆知
Dialogue: 1,0:06:23.28,0:06:25.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Flat puzzles are well known by everyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.00,0:06:28.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,但三维拼图则带来不同的挑战
Dialogue: 1,0:06:26.00,0:06:28.56,Original,,0,0,0,,but three D puzzles present a different challenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.36,0:06:33.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些三维拼图诞生于电脑之中
Dialogue: 1,0:06:29.36,0:06:33.44,Original,,0,0,0,,These three dimensional puzzles are conceived within the brain of a computer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.88,0:06:44.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,图案转印到大印刷纸后，还需制作母模切刀
Dialogue: 1,0:06:40.88,0:06:44.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Transferred to large printing sheets, a master die must be created.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.44,0:06:49.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,切割拼片需要锋利如剃刀的精密刀片
Dialogue: 1,0:06:45.44,0:06:49.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Precise, razor sharp blades are needed to cut puzzle pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.84,0:06:58.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,每个拼图都有独一无二的母模切刀
Dialogue: 1,0:06:55.84,0:06:58.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The master cutting die is unique to each puzzle.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.36,0:07:04.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,工人们仔细测量，以确保套准无误
Dialogue: 1,0:07:01.36,0:07:04.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Workers measure meticulously to obtain a perfect register.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.00,0:07:16.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,切割时模切刀绝不能移动
Dialogue: 1,0:07:14.00,0:07:16.88,Original,,0,0,0,,It's imperative that the die not move during the cutting.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.88,0:07:21.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,任何偏差都会产生灾难性的连锁反应
Dialogue: 1,0:07:18.88,0:07:21.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Any deviation would have a disastrous knock-on effect,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.84,0:07:23.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,所以要把模切刀牢牢固定到位
Dialogue: 1,0:07:21.84,0:07:23.60,Original,,0,0,0,,so it's firmly secured in its place.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.88,0:07:40.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,模切刀的复制件被安装到位
Dialogue: 1,0:07:38.88,0:07:40.56,Original,,0,0,0,,A copy of the die is positioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.36,0:07:42.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,这有点像是印刷母版
Dialogue: 1,0:07:41.36,0:07:42.88,Original,,0,0,0,,It's somewhat like printing the master.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.44,0:07:52.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,再次校验对准情况，这一步至关重要，它决定了成品的质量
Dialogue: 1,0:07:43.44,0:07:52.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Alignment is again verified, a highly important step which ensures the quality of the final product.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.44,0:07:55.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后，这块大金属板
Dialogue: 1,0:07:53.44,0:07:55.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Finally, this large metallic plate,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.68,0:07:57.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,即切割底座，被安装上去
Dialogue: 1,0:07:55.68,0:07:57.52,Original,,0,0,0,,which is the cutting base, is installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.64,0:07:59.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,就在这个表面上
Dialogue: 1,0:07:58.64,0:07:59.84,Original,,0,0,0,,It will be on this surface that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.00,0:08:01.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,母模切刀将被冲压
Dialogue: 1,0:08:00.00,0:08:01.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The master die will be struck.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.56,0:08:06.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,测量完成后，模切板被推入到位
Dialogue: 1,0:08:02.56,0:08:06.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Once measurements are finished, the draw of the die is slid into place.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.72,0:08:17.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台压力机按拼图上的图案进行切割
Dialogue: 1,0:08:14.72,0:08:17.92,Original,,0,0,0,,This press cuts the pattern as it appears on the puzzle.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.64,0:08:21.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,印刷好的纸板一张张送入模切板
Dialogue: 1,0:08:18.64,0:08:21.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The sheets or printed cardboards go into the draw one
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.60,0:08:24.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,按母版图样进行切割
Dialogue: 1,0:08:21.60,0:08:24.32,Original,,0,0,0,,by one, where they're cut according to the master model.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.68,0:08:51.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,在这个质检点，要检验切割的精确度
Dialogue: 1,0:08:47.68,0:08:51.44,Original,,0,0,0,,At this checkpoint, verification of the precision of the cut is carried out.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.16,0:08:54.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,每一块拼片都必须形状准确
Dialogue: 1,0:08:52.16,0:08:54.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Every piece must be correctly shaped.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.68,0:09:01.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是拼图的泡沫衬板
Dialogue: 1,0:08:59.68,0:09:01.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Next up is the foam support of the puzzle.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.72,0:09:05.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台裁切机用于裁切聚乙烯薄膜
Dialogue: 1,0:09:02.72,0:09:05.36,Original,,0,0,0,,This guillotine is used to cut the polythene sheets
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.52,0:09:07.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,以便粘贴切割好的图案
Dialogue: 1,0:09:05.52,0:09:07.36,Original,,0,0,0,,onto which they will glue the cut images.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.92,0:09:16.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,泡沫板送入这台覆膜机
Dialogue: 1,0:09:13.92,0:09:16.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Foam sheets are inserted into this laminator and
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.88,0:09:19.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,加热到232摄氏度
Dialogue: 1,0:09:16.88,0:09:19.68,Original,,0,0,0,,heated to 232 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.00,0:09:24.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,印有图案的薄膜用热固性粘合剂粘到泡沫板上
Dialogue: 1,0:09:20.00,0:09:24.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The sheet with the design on it is glued onto the foam with a thermosetting adhesive.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.24,0:09:29.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在把印刷薄膜贴到泡沫板上
Dialogue: 1,0:09:26.24,0:09:29.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Now they glue the printed sheet onto the foam sheet.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.16,0:09:39.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,粘合完成后，拼图被叠放起来，进入拆料工序
Dialogue: 1,0:09:34.16,0:09:39.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Once the adhesion is finished, the puzzles are stacked and they proceed to the unbuckling operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.12,0:09:43.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,通过拉拽去除多余的切料
Dialogue: 1,0:09:41.12,0:09:43.52,Original,,0,0,0,,By pulling, they remove the surplus cuttings.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.46,0:09:54.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,同一图案在一块板上印有好几份
Dialogue: 1,0:09:51.46,0:09:54.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The same design is printed several times on a sheet,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.72,0:09:56.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,所以必须把每个拼图分开
Dialogue: 1,0:09:54.72,0:09:56.40,Original,,0,0,0,,so they must separate each puzzle.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.04,0:09:59.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,这道工序叫模型拆分
Dialogue: 1,0:09:57.04,0:09:59.44,Original,,0,0,0,,This step is called the reduction of the models.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.12,0:10:08.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在要把拼片分离开来
Dialogue: 1,0:10:07.12,0:10:08.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the pieces have to be separated.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.36,0:10:13.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台分件机完成这一任务，把拼片送入滑道
Dialogue: 1,0:10:09.36,0:10:13.36,Original,,0,0,0,,This decorticator handles this task and sends the pieces down a chute.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.76,0:10:23.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,包装盒运来时已成型
Dialogue: 1,0:10:21.76,0:10:23.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Packing cartons arrive already made up,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.00,0:10:26.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,拼片被装入盒中
Dialogue: 1,0:10:24.00,0:10:26.72,Original,,0,0,0,,and the puzzle pieces are placed in their boxes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.64,0:10:31.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里每天生产15000个拼图
Dialogue: 1,0:10:28.64,0:10:31.68,Original,,0,0,0,,15,000 puzzles are produced here each day.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.32,0:10:37.50,Translation,,0,0,0,,自投产以来，该公司已设计出300多种不同的拼图
Dialogue: 1,0:10:32.32,0:10:37.50,Original,,0,0,0,,Since it began operations, the company has created more than 300 different puzzle models
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.50,0:10:40.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,从简单到极其复杂的图案不一而足
Dialogue: 1,0:10:37.50,0:10:40.00,Original,,0,0,0,,from simple to much more complex designs.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.00,0:10:46.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,其中最大的拼图共有3146块拼片
Dialogue: 1,0:10:40.00,0:10:46.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The largest of them have a total of 3,146 pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.76,0:10:53.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来的《造物小百科》：
Dialogue: 1,0:10:51.76,0:10:53.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Coming up in How It's Made:
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.04,0:11:00.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,废旧轮胎堆积如山，一直饱受诟病，这理所当然
Dialogue: 1,0:10:57.04,0:11:00.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Used tire mountains have had a bad press, and rightly so.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.80,0:11:05.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,当然，消除废物的最好办法，就是把它回收制成胶垫
Dialogue: 1,0:11:00.80,0:11:05.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Of course, the best way to eradicate waste is to recycle it into rubber mats.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.24,0:11:07.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,我们还会看看不起眼的马桶
Dialogue: 1,0:11:06.24,0:11:07.84,Original,,0,0,0,,And we look at the humble lavatory,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.24,0:11:10.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,250年来我们一直视它为理所当然
Dialogue: 1,0:11:08.24,0:11:10.80,Original,,0,0,0,,for 250 years we've taken them for granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.12,0:11:12.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,但你还会想用旱厕吗？
Dialogue: 1,0:11:11.12,0:11:12.88,Original,,0,0,0,,But would you still want to use a latrine?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.68,0:11:14.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,广告之后再见
Dialogue: 1,0:11:13.68,0:11:14.56,Original,,0,0,0,,See you after the break.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.36,0:11:26.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎回到《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:11:25.36,0:11:26.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to How It's Made.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.72,0:11:30.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍后，我们将看看不起眼的马桶
Dialogue: 1,0:11:28.72,0:11:30.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Later, we look at the humble lavatory.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.12,0:11:33.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,250年来我们一直视它为理所当然
Dialogue: 1,0:11:31.12,0:11:33.52,Original,,0,0,0,,For 250 years, we've taken them for granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.00,0:11:35.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,但你还会想用旱厕吗？
Dialogue: 1,0:11:34.00,0:11:35.68,Original,,0,0,0,,But would you still want to use a latrine?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.80,0:11:41.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,但先来看废旧轮胎，数以百万计
Dialogue: 1,0:11:36.80,0:11:41.92,Original,,0,0,0,,But first, used tires, millions of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.92,0:11:45.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些轮胎山反映了人类对道路交通工具的渴求
Dialogue: 1,0:11:41.92,0:11:45.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Mountains that reflect man's appetite for all things road-based.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.16,0:11:48.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,垃圾填埋场是自然界的祸害
Dialogue: 1,0:11:46.16,0:11:48.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Landfills are a blight on nature,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.56,0:11:51.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,消除废物的最好办法就是回收利用
Dialogue: 1,0:11:48.56,0:11:51.76,Original,,0,0,0,,and the best way to eradicate waste is to recycle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.80,0:11:56.98,Translation,,0,0,0,,轮胎正被赋予新生，变成胶垫
Dialogue: 1,0:11:52.80,0:11:56.98,Original,,0,0,0,,Tires are starting to be given a new life as rubber mats.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.68,0:12:02.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是我们对乡村的美好憧憬
Dialogue: 1,0:11:59.68,0:12:02.32,Original,,0,0,0,,This is the idyll we all have of the countryside,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.80,0:12:04.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,但有时景色也会被破坏
Dialogue: 1,0:12:02.80,0:12:04.48,Original,,0,0,0,,but sometimes the view can be spoiled.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.04,0:12:08.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一堆大约有10万个轮胎
Dialogue: 1,0:12:05.04,0:12:08.24,Original,,0,0,0,,There are around 100,000 tires in this pile.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.88,0:12:15.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,好在这些轮胎将重获新生，变成胶垫
Dialogue: 1,0:12:10.88,0:12:15.44,Original,,0,0,0,,But thankfully these tires will have a second life as rubber mats.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.08,0:12:20.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂每天回收15000个轮胎
Dialogue: 1,0:12:16.08,0:12:20.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Each day in this factory, they recycle 15,000 tires.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.36,0:12:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,轮胎必须被分解成小颗粒
Dialogue: 1,0:12:23.36,0:12:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Tires have to be reduced to little granules.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.40,0:12:29.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先，传送带把轮胎送入清洗机
Dialogue: 1,0:12:26.40,0:12:29.36,Original,,0,0,0,,but first this conveyor feeds the tires into the washer.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.36,0:12:33.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,轮胎清洗后送入破碎机
Dialogue: 1,0:12:31.36,0:12:33.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Tires are washed and then sent to the shredder.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.44,0:12:41.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,破碎机有两排巨大的刀齿
Dialogue: 1,0:12:38.44,0:12:41.12,Original,,0,0,0,,The shredder, with its 2 rows of large teeth,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.36,0:12:45.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,能轻松对付卡车轮胎，把它们碾成碎块
Dialogue: 1,0:12:41.36,0:12:45.20,Original,,0,0,0,,makes short work of the lorry tyres and grinds them up into pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.00,0:12:53.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台破碎机每小时能破碎近1000个轮胎
Dialogue: 1,0:12:50.00,0:12:53.52,Original,,0,0,0,,This shredder is able to cut up almost 1,000 tyres an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.72,0:12:56.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着进行第二次破碎
Dialogue: 1,0:12:54.72,0:12:56.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Then, the shredder a second time.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.68,0:13:10.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,用强力磁铁把金属从橡胶中分离出来，金属碎片
Dialogue: 1,0:13:05.68,0:13:10.00,Original,,0,0,0,,With huge magnets, metal is separated from the rubber and the metal pieces
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.08,0:13:11.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,会被另一家工厂回收利用
Dialogue: 1,0:13:10.08,0:13:11.92,Original,,0,0,0,,are recycled at another factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.00,0:13:20.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,轮胎中的其他成分，如玻璃纤维和尼龙，也必须分离出来
Dialogue: 1,0:13:16.00,0:13:20.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Other components of the tyres, such as fiberglass and nylon, also have to be separated.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.20,0:13:23.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,用筛分机去除剩余的杂物
Dialogue: 1,0:13:21.20,0:13:23.84,Original,,0,0,0,,A sifter is used to get out the remaining debris.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.32,0:13:30.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,这座回收料场堆放着16吨轮胎颗粒
Dialogue: 1,0:13:26.32,0:13:30.08,Original,,0,0,0,,16 tons of tyre particles are piled up in this recycling depot,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.04,0:13:37.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,但颗粒仍然太大，无法使用
Dialogue: 1,0:13:35.04,0:13:37.52,Original,,0,0,0,,but the pellets are still too large to be used.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.24,0:13:40.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们被送入二次破碎机
Dialogue: 1,0:13:38.24,0:13:40.00,Original,,0,0,0,,They're sent to a secondary shredder,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.40,0:13:41.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,在那里被进一步粉碎
Dialogue: 1,0:13:40.40,0:13:41.92,Original,,0,0,0,,where they'll be reduced even further.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.00,0:13:59.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,强烈的研磨作用产生出橡胶粉末
Dialogue: 1,0:13:56.00,0:13:59.52,Original,,0,0,0,,The intense grinding action produces a kind of rubber powder.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.96,0:14:11.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,粉末被摊铺在这些巨大的模具上
Dialogue: 1,0:14:08.96,0:14:11.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The powder is spread out on these enormous moulds.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.08,0:14:14.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,它有7米长，1米多宽
Dialogue: 1,0:14:12.08,0:14:14.72,Original,,0,0,0,,It's 7 metres long and just over a metre wide.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.72,0:14:21.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后存放在压力机的装料架中
Dialogue: 1,0:14:18.72,0:14:21.44,Original,,0,0,0,,They're then stored in this loading magazine of the press.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.92,0:14:24.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,装满后，模具被送入胶垫压机
Dialogue: 1,0:14:21.92,0:14:24.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Once full, the moulds are sent to the rubber mat press.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.20,0:14:38.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,在压机内，粉末要在高温下压制30分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:14:33.20,0:14:38.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Within this mat press, the powder has to be cooked at high temperatures for 30 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.20,0:14:47.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,压制成型的胶垫经脱模装置取出，送去冷却
Dialogue: 1,0:14:43.20,0:14:47.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The cooked mat goes through the un-moulding unit before being sent off to cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.52,0:14:53.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,此时的胶垫仍然非常烫
Dialogue: 1,0:14:51.52,0:14:53.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The rubber mats are still extremely hot.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.40,0:14:57.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,用水流喷淋冷却几分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:14:54.40,0:14:57.20,Original,,0,0,0,,They're cooled with jets of water for a period of several minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.42,0:15:08.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,冷却后的胶垫现在可以送往下一道工序
Dialogue: 1,0:15:05.42,0:15:08.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The cooled mats can now be sent to the next department.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.04,0:15:12.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,切割中心的传送带在切割前先对胶垫定位
Dialogue: 1,0:15:09.04,0:15:12.64,Original,,0,0,0,,This conveyor in the cutting centre positions the mat before it's cut.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.44,0:15:16.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,胶垫通过振动去除多余水分
Dialogue: 1,0:15:13.44,0:15:16.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The mat is vibrated to eliminate any surplus water.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.24,0:15:25.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在每张胶垫被切成3块
Dialogue: 1,0:15:22.24,0:15:25.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Each rubber mat is now cut up into 3 pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.16,0:15:36.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,切好的胶垫堆叠存放，等待发货
Dialogue: 1,0:15:32.16,0:15:36.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The cut mats are then stacked into a pile and stored before being shipped.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.92,0:15:43.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里还生产挡泥板
Dialogue: 1,0:15:41.92,0:15:43.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Mud guards are also made here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.64,0:15:46.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们的制作方法与胶垫相同
Dialogue: 1,0:15:44.64,0:15:46.88,Original,,0,0,0,,These are made in the same way as the other mats.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.84,0:15:49.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,在水中冷却后
Dialogue: 1,0:15:47.84,0:15:49.36,Original,,0,0,0,,After having been cooled in water,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.68,0:15:54.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,趁余温尚在，通过开缺口工序去除多余橡胶
Dialogue: 1,0:15:49.68,0:15:54.88,Original,,0,0,0,,but while they're still warm, they remove the surplus rubber in an operation called notching.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.36,0:16:06.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂还生产硬橡胶圈
Dialogue: 1,0:16:03.36,0:16:06.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Hard rubber rings are also produced at this factory
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.24,0:16:07.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,采用相同的制造工艺
Dialogue: 1,0:16:06.24,0:16:07.92,Original,,0,0,0,,with the same fabrication methods,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.16,0:16:10.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,原料照例是废旧轮胎
Dialogue: 1,0:16:08.16,0:16:10.72,Original,,0,0,0,,and as always, from old used tyres.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.80,0:16:19.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,在12小时内，这家工厂至少能生产12000张
Dialogue: 1,0:16:14.80,0:16:19.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Over a 12-hour period, this facility makes no less than 12,000
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.04,0:16:21.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,用回收旧轮胎制成的胶垫
Dialogue: 1,0:16:19.04,0:16:21.12,Original,,0,0,0,,rubber mats from old recycled tyres.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.76,0:16:23.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这对公司来说是笔好生意
Dialogue: 1,0:16:21.76,0:16:23.20,Original,,0,0,0,,It's good business for the company,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.68,0:16:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,最终对所有人也都有好处
Dialogue: 1,0:16:23.68,0:16:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,and ultimately for everyone else too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.60,0:16:34.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,生活中，我们总是不自觉地忽视那些让生活更便利的东西
Dialogue: 1,0:16:29.60,0:16:34.56,Original,,0,0,0,,In life, we invariably take for granted the things that make our lives more convenient.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.44,0:16:36.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,就拿马桶来说
Dialogue: 1,0:16:35.44,0:16:36.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Take the lavatory.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.72,0:16:41.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,自1775年以来，冲水马桶一直没什么大的变化
Dialogue: 1,0:16:36.72,0:16:41.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Since 1775, the flushing toilet has remained. Pretty much the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.76,0:16:44.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,如此寻常的器具，却承担着重任
Dialogue: 1,0:16:41.76,0:16:44.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Such a humble appliance, and such a big job to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.36,0:16:54.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,在雕塑工作室的底座上，一件作品正在制作中
Dialogue: 1,0:16:49.36,0:16:54.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Based upon a plinth in a sculptor's studio, a piece of work is in progress.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.64,0:16:56.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过，这可不是罗丹的作品
Dialogue: 1,0:16:54.64,0:16:56.32,Original,,0,0,0,,However, this is no Rodin.
Dialogue: 2,0:16:54.64,0:16:57.39,Annotation,,0,0,0,,罗丹：法国著名雕塑大师
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.28,0:17:01.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,制作马桶的第一步，是组装几块模具
Dialogue: 1,0:16:57.28,0:17:01.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The initial stage in creating a lavatory is to assemble several moulds.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.92,0:17:05.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,每款新产品都要设计一个母石膏模
Dialogue: 1,0:17:01.92,0:17:05.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Each new product requires the design of a master plaster mould
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.60,0:17:09.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,再据此制作塑料工具模或母模
Dialogue: 1,0:17:05.60,0:17:09.04,Original,,0,0,0,,from which they will produce a plastic tool or master.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.08,0:17:12.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,用它来制作批量石膏模
Dialogue: 1,0:17:10.08,0:17:12.88,Original,,0,0,0,,This will be used to create plaster duplicates.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.60,0:17:28.54,Translation,,0,0,0,,马桶的石膏生产模由6块不同的分片组成
Dialogue: 1,0:17:23.60,0:17:28.54,Original,,0,0,0,,The plaster production mould of a toilet is made from 6 different segmented pieces
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.54,0:17:29.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,需要逐一拼装
Dialogue: 1,0:17:28.54,0:17:29.68,Original,,0,0,0,,which have to be assembled.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.36,0:17:35.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先按精确配比混合水和石膏
Dialogue: 1,0:17:31.36,0:17:35.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The process begins with a mixture of water and plaster according to a precise recipe.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.40,0:17:39.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后把石膏浆从工具模的注入口倒入
Dialogue: 1,0:17:36.40,0:17:39.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the liquid is poured into this filling hole of the tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.16,0:17:43.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,石膏凝固后，就可以开始脱模
Dialogue: 1,0:17:40.16,0:17:43.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Once the plaster hardens, they can then proceed with the unmoulding.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.32,0:17:46.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,用橡胶锤把石膏模与外围分离
Dialogue: 1,0:17:44.32,0:17:46.56,Original,,0,0,0,,They separate the plaster mould from the surround with
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.56,0:17:49.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,以免造成损伤
Dialogue: 1,0:17:46.56,0:17:49.04,Original,,0,0,0,,a rubber hammer so as not to cause any damage.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.04,0:18:02.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,各分片被轻轻拼合
Dialogue: 1,0:18:01.04,0:18:02.72,Original,,0,0,0,,The pieces are gently assembled,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.96,0:18:05.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,马桶的雏形逐渐显现
Dialogue: 1,0:18:02.96,0:18:05.44,Original,,0,0,0,,and the toilet softly takes its shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.40,0:18:18.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后安装张紧带
Dialogue: 1,0:18:16.40,0:18:18.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Then they install tensioning straps.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.88,0:18:22.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,在模具和张紧带之间插入小木块以增加张力
Dialogue: 1,0:18:18.88,0:18:22.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Little blocks are inserted between the mould and the strap to increase the tension.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.76,0:18:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,模具很快就要注入泥浆
Dialogue: 1,0:18:23.76,0:18:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The mould will soon be filled with liquid,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.92,0:18:28.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,木块可防止模具变形
Dialogue: 1,0:18:25.92,0:18:28.32,Original,,0,0,0,,and the blocks prevent any distortion occurring.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.04,0:18:31.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,在大桶中正在调配泥浆
Dialogue: 1,0:18:29.04,0:18:31.68,Original,,0,0,0,,In massive vats, the recipe is being prepared.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.48,0:18:35.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种被称为泥浆的原料由黏土和二氧化硅组成
Dialogue: 1,0:18:32.48,0:18:35.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Known as slip, this is a composite of clay and silica.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.40,0:18:39.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着安装型芯，即模具的上部
Dialogue: 1,0:18:36.40,0:18:39.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Now they install the core, the upper part of the mould.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.48,0:18:42.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在可以开始注浆了
Dialogue: 1,0:18:40.48,0:18:42.08,Original,,0,0,0,,They can now proceed with the filling.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.48,0:18:47.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这根铜制分流管连接着泥浆罐
Dialogue: 1,0:18:44.48,0:18:47.92,Original,,0,0,0,,This copper distribution pipe, connected to the tank containing the slip,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.16,0:18:50.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,可同时向多个模具注浆
Dialogue: 1,0:18:48.16,0:18:50.40,Original,,0,0,0,,allows the filling of several moulds at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.04,0:18:54.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,每个模具大约需要20公斤泥浆
Dialogue: 1,0:18:51.04,0:18:54.08,Original,,0,0,0,,About 20 kilos of the mix per mould is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.48,0:19:03.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,1小时后，泥浆已凝结到1厘米厚
Dialogue: 1,0:19:00.48,0:19:03.84,Original,,0,0,0,,After an hour, the slip has attained a thickness of 1 centimeter,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.16,0:19:08.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,拔掉塞子，让多余的泥浆流出
Dialogue: 1,0:19:04.16,0:19:08.96,Original,,0,0,0,,and the plug is pulled to allow the excess slip to run out.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.20,0:19:11.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在可以脱模取出还易碎的坯体
Dialogue: 1,0:19:09.20,0:19:11.84,Original,,0,0,0,,They can now unmold the still fragile piece.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.96,0:19:16.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,用较稠的泥浆把这两部分粘合起来
Dialogue: 1,0:19:12.96,0:19:16.08,Original,,0,0,0,,This thicker slip is used to adhere these 2 pieces together.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.60,0:19:30.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,他们开好孔，把整体分离开
Dialogue: 1,0:19:27.60,0:19:30.24,Original,,0,0,0,,They cut the holes and disengage the ensemble.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.72,0:19:32.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,马桶至此成型
Dialogue: 1,0:19:30.72,0:19:32.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The toilet is now moulded.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.76,0:19:37.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,为了获得完美的外观
Dialogue: 1,0:19:35.76,0:19:37.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Then, to obtain a perfect appearance,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.84,0:19:41.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,要去掉粘合泥浆溢出形成的小棱边
Dialogue: 1,0:19:37.84,0:19:41.36,Original,,0,0,0,,they remove the little ridge formed by the surplus adhesive slip.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.08,0:19:50.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,马桶先自然风干36小时
Dialogue: 1,0:19:48.08,0:19:50.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The toilet air-dries for 36 hours,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.72,0:19:53.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,再放入温热烘干机烘干12小时
Dialogue: 1,0:19:50.72,0:19:53.20,Original,,0,0,0,,then in a warm air-dryer for 12 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.60,0:19:57.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,表面修整必须一丝不苟
Dialogue: 1,0:19:55.60,0:19:57.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Finishing must be impeccable.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.24,0:20:00.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,他们仔细打磨表面，使其光滑如镜
Dialogue: 1,0:19:58.24,0:20:00.96,Original,,0,0,0,,They carefully sand the surface to make it perfectly smooth.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.68,0:20:03.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,用吸尘器吸走粉尘
Dialogue: 1,0:20:01.68,0:20:03.52,Original,,0,0,0,,A vacuum cleaner draws up the dust.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.96,0:20:08.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,再用压缩空气把粉尘和碎屑吹净
Dialogue: 1,0:20:04.96,0:20:08.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Then, with a jet of compressed air, dust and debris are blown away.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.24,0:20:13.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,座便器随后由手工上釉
Dialogue: 1,0:20:12.24,0:20:13.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Bowls are then hand-painted.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.56,0:20:22.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,水箱则由机器人喷涂上釉
Dialogue: 1,0:20:19.56,0:20:22.44,Original,,0,0,0,,As for the cistern tanks, they are painted by a robot.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.32,0:20:39.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后卡车把各部件运往最后一道工序
Dialogue: 1,0:20:35.32,0:20:39.52,Original,,0,0,0,,A truck then carries the different parts to the final fabrication stage.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.52,0:20:40.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,高温烧制
Dialogue: 1,0:20:39.52,0:20:40.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Baking.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.20,0:20:50.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,马桶在这个窑炉中，在1176摄氏度的高温下烧制23小时
Dialogue: 1,0:20:43.20,0:20:50.72,Original,,0,0,0,,The toilets remain in this oven at a very high temperature of 1,176 degrees centigrade for 23 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.44,0:20:53.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,黏土和二氧化硅需要这么长时间才能烧结
Dialogue: 1,0:20:51.44,0:20:53.84,Original,,0,0,0,,It takes this long to fuse the clay and silica.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.76,0:20:58.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,釉面变得坚硬而光亮
Dialogue: 1,0:20:56.76,0:20:58.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The paint then becomes hard and shiny,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.20,0:21:01.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,成品焕然一新，光彩夺目
Dialogue: 1,0:20:59.20,0:21:01.60,Original,,0,0,0,,and the finished article stands proud and new.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.52,0:21:09.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,历经4天工时、一位雕塑家和20公斤泥浆
Dialogue: 1,0:21:05.52,0:21:09.76,Original,,0,0,0,,After 4 days of labour, a sculptor and 20 kilos of slip,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.24,0:21:15.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,这只马桶准备好履行那个我们都习以为常的职责了
Dialogue: 1,0:21:10.24,0:21:15.36,Original,,0,0,0,,the lavatory is ready to carry on its job that we all take for granted.
